10-790 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We use our part named MyPart with the default settings.
Back to Work with Automatic Routing of the Transporter
Program the Control for Unloading the Transporter
In this step we program our control for unloading the Transporter. We do this in the method named
unload. This control is going to be called when the Transporter has reached its Destination.
The unload control unloads the part from the bed of the Transporter, assigns the now empty Transporter
to the LoadingStation as new Destination and removes the Destination Control, DestCtrl. In addition
the control writes the name of the Transporter, the previous destination, and the new destination to the
Console.
Our source code looks like this:
@.deleteMovables
print @,":"
print "Previous destination: ",@.Destination // write the previous
                                             // destination to the Console
@.Destination := LoadingStation
@.DestCtrl := ""
print "New destination: ",@.Destination      // write the new 
                                             // destination to the Console
@.move
