Cover a Route Along Omnidirectional Markers
In this simple sample model the AGV covers the set route along omnidirectional markers. This means
that it does not drive across the markers but turns in front of the marker toward the next marker. Plant
Simulation computes the curve, which the AGV drives, according to the angle of the connecting line
between the current marker and the next marker.
The finished simulation model looks like this:
Cover a Route Along Omnidirectional Markers
