Prevent AGVs from Colliding
In this model we demonstrate how to use the settings of the Distance Control of the Transporter to
prevent two AGVs from colliding.
The finished simulation model looks like this.
Prevent AGVs from Colliding
Plant Simulation Help 10-833
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Proceed as follows to create the model:
• Insert an AGVPool that creates the AGVs.
• Insert four Markers each for each of the two Transporters. Transporter1 covers the markers M11, M12,
M13, and M14. Transporter2 covers the markers M21, M22, M23, and M24.
• Insert an init control that finds an idle AGV in the AGVPool that can do the job. In addition we set the
routes of the AGVs.
Then configure the objects.
• We use the default setting of the AGVPool, meaning that the AGV is the Transporter in the folder MUs.
Prevent AGVs from Colliding
10-834 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We use the default settings for the Safety Zones of the Transporter.
• We use the default settings of the Distance Control that we created.
Prevent AGVs from Colliding
Plant Simulation Help 10-835
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We programmed the init control that finds an idle AGV in the AGVPool and sets the routes which the
AGVs cover.
var AGV1 := AGVPool.getIdleAGV
AGV1.setRoute([M11, M12, M13, M14])
wait 2
var AGV2 := AGVPool.getIdleAGV
AGV2.setRoute([M21, M22, M23, M24])
When you run the simulation, you can watch how Transporter2 slows down once Transporter1 enters its
Safety Zone 2 and then stops when it enters Safety Zone 1. Transporter2 continues on its route once
Transporter1 passed by safely.
Prevent AGVs from Colliding
10-836 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To show the defined Safety Zones of the Transporter, select Edit 3D Properties > Tab Appearance >
Show Safety Zones.
When you move the markers M11 and M12 to the left in the X-Direction, meaning that Transporter2 now
arrives first at the point where the routes cross, Transporter1 slows down and stops to let Transporter2
pass. This shows that the safety zone settings and the Distance Control reliably prevent the AGVs from
colliding.
Prevent AGVs from Colliding
