Modeling a Battery-powered Transporter, Basic
Model a Battery-powered Transporter, Basic
In this sample model we demonstrate how easy it is to quickly model a battery-powered Transporter.
The Transporters drive on a Track moving parts from one point to another. The Exit Control of the Track
detects the charge of the battery; if enough power is left, it continues moving parts, if not, it drives onto
the Track to the charging station, which charges the battery.
The finished simulation model looks like this:
Modeling a Battery-powered Transporter, Basic
10-838 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

First we duplicated the Transporter in the Class Library and renamed it to TransporterBattery.
• We selected these settings on the tab Battery:
Model a Battery-powered Transporter, Basic
Plant Simulation Help 10-839
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We typed in these instructions into the Charge Control:
if @.BatCharge >= @.BatCapacity
   @.Stopped := false
end
Then we modeled the material flow and configured the material flow objects:
Model a Battery-powered Transporter, Basic
10-840 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We selected these settings in the Source which feeds the Transporters into the plant.
Model a Battery-powered Transporter, Basic
Plant Simulation Help 10-841
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We created an Exit Control in the object Track, which sends a Transporter with a low battery charge on
the Track, ChargeBattery in our case, that leads to the charging station.
We typed in this source code:
if @.BatCharge <= @.BatReserve
   @.move(1)
else
   @.move(2)
end
• We created two Sensors on the object Track and selected these settings.
Model a Battery-powered Transporter, Basic
10-842 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

At the sensor with the ID 3 the TransferStation loads the parts onto the loading space of the
Transporter.
At the sensor with the ID 1 the PickAndPlace robot unloads the parts from the loading space of the
Transporter and places them on the Conveyor at the sensor. We typed in these instructions into the
Sensor Control OnSensor1.
param SensorID: integer, Front: boolean, BookPos: boolean
// Activating the sensor moves the parts on to the designated
// destination, namely the PickAndPlace robot.
@.Stopped := true
var Destination:object := PickAndPlace
while not @.Empty
   var MU: object := @.cont
   if not MU.move(Destination)
      stopuntil MU.Location /= @ and not Destination.IsLoading
   end
Model a Battery-powered Transporter, Basic
