We did not change other settings.
Excursus: The relative and the absolute path
For the Charge Control we just entered its name into the text box. Once we click Apply, Plant Simulation
highlights the text box in red as it does not find the charge control within the namespace of the Class
Library with the specified relative path. We accept that though as the Transporters are created in our
Frame named Model and are thus located within the same namespace as the Charge Control.
Excursus: The relative and the absolute path
Plant Simulation Help 10-851
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
If we click the 
  button in the dialog of the Transporter, navigate to the Frame named Model,
and select the charge control in the dialog Select Object, Plant Simulation inserts the relative path
(designated by the tilde ~) to the charge control within the namespace of the Frame.
When we then run the simulation, Plant Simulation notifies us that the charge control does not exist in
the class of the object within the namespace of the Class Library.
When we select the check box Absolute Path, Plant Simulation enters the absolute path (designated by
the asterisk *) to the charge control. In this case Plant Simulation runs the simulation without errors. If
we then rename the Frame, the absolute path will no longer work though. For this reason the relative
path is to be preferred in most cases.
Excursus: The relative and the absolute path
10-852 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

