Back to Model a Battery-powered Transporter, Extended
Program the Battery Controls
In the last step we program the Charge Control myBatteryChargeControl. It charges the battery and then,
once it is fully charged, moves the Transporter onto the ParkingPosition.
// battery charge control of the Transporter, recognizes that the battery 
has to be charge, 
// once the charge is smaller than or equal to the battery reserve
if @.BatCharge <~= @.BatReserve 
   @.BatCharging := true   // start charging the battery
   @.transfer(ChargingStation)
elseif  @.BatCharge >~= @.BatCapacity
   @.move(ParkingPosition)  // move Transporter with charged battery to 
ParkingPosition
end
Lastly we program the Entrance Control of the ChargingStation. It moves the fully charged Transporter
from the ParkingPosition onto the Track.
// entrance control of the ParkingPosition
waituntil ParkingPosition.NumMU > 0 prio 1
ParkingPosition.Cont.move(Track, 9)
When we now run the simulation, we can trace how the Transporters circulate and first move onto the
ChargingStation when the battery charge is low and then move on to the ParkingPosition.
Program the Battery Controls
